reviewer_concerns.value:
Main concerns from reviewers include:

1. MI-based layer pairing and RFM choices feel ad hoc / weakly justified;

2. Limited mechanistic/causal analysis; dependence on expert quality and sizable labeled data;

3. Hyperparameter search and per-pair adapters weaken “lightweight/model-agnostic” claims;

4. Missing stronger PEFT baselines (e.g., LoRA); limited large-model/robustness evaluation.
